<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Datong</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Pingcheng</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Datong is a city in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shanxi">Shanxi</a> province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-wall-of-china">Great Wall</a>. As Pingcheng it was the capital of the Northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cao-wei">Wei dynasty</a> from 398 until the move to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luoyang">Luoyang</a> in 494, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yungang-grottoes">Yungang Grottoes</a> were carved nearby. Later one of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sixteen-prefectures">Sixteen Prefectures</a> ceded to the Khitan, it was the Western Capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty">Liao</a> and Jin dynasties, and in modern times it became a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">coal</a>-mining centre.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/datong.jpg" alt="Datong" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: xiquinhosilva · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Datong_Ancient_City_Wall_(54578074197).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
